    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I've got a heifer that just came out of rumenotomy about 6 hours ago. I need a clear protocol for what I should be looking out for over the next few days regarding the incision site and any internal signs of trouble or infection. Also, what's the plan for getting her back on feed?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For the incision site, monitor closely for excessive swelling, redness, heat, or discharge, as these can indicate infection. Look for lameness, lethargy, or a sustained high fever, which suggest deeper complications. Regarding diet, start her on easily digestible, low-fiber feed as recommended by your veterinarian to minimize digestive stress. Gradually increase the feed amount over the next 24-48 hours, ensuring she maintains good appetite.",
      "source": "target",
